the kansas city chiefs are already very  well positioned for the postseason with  patrick mahomes and i think we've seen  time and again  in patrick mahomes 20 nfl starts that he  truly is a special talent maybe the best  quarterback we've ever seen now that  doesn't mean he's going to continue to  play that way but he kind of is who he  is he moves the way he does he throws  the way he does barring injury this guy  is going to continue to be  special in a way that we've never  witnessed so  i saw some talk renewed yesterday about  what his contract will be worth the next  time he signs a deal with the chiefs  he's still operating under the terms of  the contract that he signed as the 10th  overall pick back in 2017. and adam  schefter of espn has mentioned a couple  times now back in january the first time  and yesterday the most recent that  mahomes will sign a deal worth 200  million or more and that really isn't a  shock because it'll be a five-year  extension worth 40 million a year you do  the math that's 200 million dollars the  question is how much will be gained  guaranteed what will the full structure  be and more importantly  when will they do this deal because  people think that a player isn't  eligible for a contract until his third  season ends and they're right but the  key word is third regular season and  there are people in the league who don't  know this because i've had the  conversation i said look here's the page  of the cba where it says completion of  the third regular season the day after  week 17 the chiefs and patrick mahomes  could sign a long-term contract and if  i'm mahomes if i'm his agents i'm laying  the foundation now to tell the team i  want that contract the day after the end  of the regular season the money you get  playing those postseason games is  peanuts in comparison to what you make  in your game checks and it's definitely  peanuts in comparison to what he would  make on a new contract why put your  future payday at risk through extra  postseason games when the window is  already open on a long-term deal that's  what he needs to be pushing for now will  the chiefs comply when we interviewed  clark hunt the owner of the chiefs back  in march he said we've got some  opportunities and we're keenly aware of  the fact that when you have a young  quarterback the cap burden allows you to  build the team around him  so they may not be budgeting  a big contract for patrick mahomes until  we get into 2020 until after march but  if they're wise they will clear out cap  space now they will have enough left  over that they can sign patrick mahomes  to his new deal during the 2019 league  year and as soon as the 2019 regular  season ends because mahomes deserves it  and he should be clamoring for it and  look there's no real leverage here  because it's not like he's going to walk  out but at the same time the right thing  to do given the special talent that the  chiefs now have and that they hope to  have for the next 10 15 20 years get him  taken care of financially as soon as  possible and the first possible day is  the day after the 2019 regular season  ends actually it's after the game ends  do it that night have it ready to go  that's what the chiefs should do because  when you have a great player you need to  recognize it and you need to act  accordingly and mahomes great guy hasn't  changed incredible quarterback it would  be very wise of the chiefs to pay him  what he's worth the moment that they're  able to do so that's it for today's pft  ot check us out all weekend long at  profootballtalk.com we'll be back on  monday with another edition of pft live  more pft pms coming throughout the week  but for now the focus is on week four  and we will do everything we can to get  you ready to go for all the action that  is to come have a great weekend and  we'll talk monday  [Music]  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

